bibit-runtime-plugin (0.1.27) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Keep the external-service adapter alive through a stray SIGTERM.  systemd
    treats SIGTERM as a clean exit, so `Restart=on-failure` left the unit dead
    after any `pkill -f real_runtime_proxy.py` -- the same script the
    documented development preview runs -- and every Runtime page in Bi-bit
    then reported the service as offline until someone restarted the unit by
    hand.  The unit now uses `Restart=always`, and the preview instructions
    stop it by PID instead of by process name.
  * Show the recovery command when the host reports the Runtime as offline.
    Page loads rendered the host's own "The service is offline" placeholder;
    they now go through the same translator as the mutation paths, which names
    bibit-runtime-adapter@bianbu.service and the systemctl command that
    restores it, in both languages.

